---
title: Workout blocks
description: "Add a kind of block to LogIt workouts, like timed rounds or hangboard hangs: a JSON declaration, no code."
---

A workout block plugin adds a **kind of block** to workouts, next to Strength, Cardio and
Mobility: rounds of rolling or sparring, hangboard hangs, climbing problems. You describe the
block; LogIt draws it, times it and keeps it in history. It's pure JSON, no code, so it
installs whether or not community plugins are turned on.

Coaches put blocks in programs (Programs › a day › **+ From a plugin**), with the block's
settings and how many entries it starts with ("6 rounds"). Their client is asked to allow it
the first time; until they do, the block is a note in their workout.

## The block file

The file is the declaration itself, and its `id` is the plugin's id.

```json
{
  "id": "com.you.rounds",
  "name": "Rounds",
  "description": "Timed rounds with rest and notes.",
  "entry": { "one": "Round", "many": "Rounds" },
  "blockFields": [
    { "key": "kind", "type": "choice", "label": "What", "options": ["Rolling", "Sparring"], "remember": true }
  ],
  "fields": [
    { "key": "length", "type": "duration", "label": "Length", "default": 300, "timer": "work", "column": true },
    { "key": "partner", "type": "text", "label": "Partner", "optional": true, "suggestions": "previous", "column": true },
    { "key": "note", "type": "text", "label": "Note", "multiline": true, "optional": true }
  ],
  "timer": { "pattern": "rounds", "work": "length", "rest": { "default": 60, "label": "Rest" } },
  "summary": "{count} rounds"
}
```

- **`entry`**: what one entry is called, and several.
- **`fields`**: what each entry records (a round, a hang). **`blockFields`**: set once for the
  whole block (gi or no-gi, which board). Coaches fill in the block fields in a program.
- Field types: `number`, `weight`, `distance`, `duration` (seconds), `counter`, `scale`
  (with `min`/`max`), `choice` and `tags` (with `options`, or `"list:<id>"` for one of your
  `lists`), `toggle`, `text`.
- Field options: `optional`, `default`, `unit`, `step`, `min`, `max`, `remember` (prefill from
  the last block), `suggestions: "previous"`, `column` (show it in the entries table), and
  `timer: "work"` on the duration the timer runs.
- **`timer`**: `none`, or `rounds` with a work field and a rest.
- **`summary`**: the line in history, with `{count}` and `{sum:<key>}`.
- **`lists`** (optional): your own lists, e.g. submissions or grades,
  `{ "grades": { "label": "Font grades", "items": ["5", "6A"], "ordered": true } }`.
- At most 20 fields. Keys are stable: a later version can add fields and rename labels, and
  rename a key with `"was": "oldKey"`, but never change a key's type.

LogIt's own blocks, Rounds and Hangboard, are good ones to copy.
